<title>USA: Astoria names CEO Engelke chairman.</title>
<headline>Astoria names CEO Engelke chairman.</headline>
<dateline>LAKE SUCCESS, N.Y. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Astoria Financial Corp said Wednesday that its president and chief executive officer, George Engelke Jr, has been elected chairman of the company and its unit, Astoria Federal Savings and Loan Association.</p>
<p>Engelke, 58, succeeds Henry Drewitz as chairman. Drewitz, 75, retired Wednesday after 50 years with the company.</p>
<p>Astoria Financial has assets of $7.7 billion. Astoria Federal, established in 1888, has 45 retail banking offices in New York.</p>
